Date: Mon, 23 Aug 1993 17:40:26 -0400 (EDT)
From: Larry Marso <lmarso@panix.com>
Subject: INVEST: what to do with just a little money?

Invest in a no-load mutual fund that closely tracks the S&P 500 index.
Call 18005551212 and get numbers for Fidelity and for Vanguard, which
market such funds.  Your state managed pension probably invests in a
conservative portfolio of assets; it is typically appropriate for someone
in your age bracket to invest in equities for the additional upside
(seeking capital appreciation rather than capital preservation).

A no-load fund means you pay no % of money invested fee to participate. 
Management fees are small.  You can withdraw your money after a short
period of time (6 months or so) without penalty, and we're only talking
about a $25 fee or thereabouts if you change your mind more quickly.

The suggested strategy depends on your willingness to leave these funds
invested over the long term.

(No, I'm not in the money management business).



